WEBVTT

01:30.800 --> 01:34.520
=Lady Liberty=

01:35.020 --> 01:37.940
=Episode 6=

01:44.660 --> 01:45.140
Thank you.

01:47.220 --> 01:47.740
Ms. Lin.

01:48.133 --> 01:51.088
(Signed Author Copyright Agreement)
I wrote a draft for "Drunk Old Friend".

01:51.500 --> 01:52.500
Could you please tell me

01:53.500 --> 01:56.100
exactly how my writing
was worse than Gu Yan's?

01:56.288 --> 01:57.888
You didn't write worse than him.

01:59.300 --> 02:01.660
You actually wrote
a better opening than he did.

02:02.540 --> 02:04.020
It's just that he wrote faster.

02:04.740 --> 02:07.300
But I was brought
into the project later than he was.

02:07.620 --> 02:08.420
I didn't expect

02:08.420 --> 02:10.340
this project to be
pushed forward so suddenly.

02:10.866 --> 02:12.740
I thought there'd be
three or four months left.

02:13.020 --> 02:14.260
If that had been the case,

02:15.020 --> 02:15.844
maybe I would've

02:16.340 --> 02:17.060
chosen you,

02:17.660 --> 02:19.700
and had Gu Yan
drop this project for something else.

02:20.780 --> 02:22.500
So this isn't fair at all.

02:29.180 --> 02:30.660
In a sense,

02:31.460 --> 02:32.340
it is fair.

02:34.940 --> 02:35.820
In the face of fate.

02:41.380 --> 02:42.820
No one must know

02:42.820 --> 02:43.650
you did a test draft

02:43.660 --> 02:44.740
for Drunk Old Friend.

02:45.940 --> 02:47.300
That's the first agreement.

02:48.420 --> 02:49.340
As for the second one,

02:49.620 --> 02:50.580
after you sign it,

02:50.700 --> 02:52.888
I'll show you
the proposal for the second story.

02:54.260 --> 02:56.220
Will it be two people
competing again this time?

02:57.180 --> 02:58.260
There are five.

02:58.420 --> 02:59.900
There are four others.

03:00.260 --> 03:02.580
But they already
started writing a few days ago.

03:03.860 --> 03:04.610
Ms. Lin,

03:04.610 --> 03:06.711
other companies
don't do pitch competitions like this.

03:06.820 --> 03:08.355
You can write better than they can.

03:12.580 --> 03:13.220
Show him.

03:14.740 --> 03:15.733
This is the proposal.

03:16.780 --> 03:17.780
Can I read it now?

03:17.780 --> 03:19.860
Don't I need to sign
a non-disclosure agreement?

03:19.980 --> 03:22.044
Read it.
You won't be able to turn it down.

03:23.020 --> 03:23.780
Stay with him.

03:23.860 --> 03:24.990
I need to go pick someone up.

03:25.180 --> 03:26.088
Thank you, Ms. Lin.

03:37.140 --> 03:37.740
Guys!

03:38.340 --> 03:39.020
Did you hear?

03:39.066 --> 03:40.500
Gu Yan is coming to the office soon.

03:40.980 --> 03:41.980
I heard about it.

03:42.100 --> 03:43.700
The 10 AM meeting is to introduce him.

03:45.420 --> 03:46.020
When did

03:46.020 --> 03:47.260
Ms. Lin start

03:47.260 --> 03:48.300
training Gu Yan?

03:48.660 --> 03:49.911
It's been at least a year.

03:50.620 --> 03:51.340
I'm guessing

03:51.980 --> 03:52.940
that if Ling Yikai

03:52.940 --> 03:55.140
and Zhao Lanxin
hadn't suddenly jumped ship,

03:56.460 --> 03:57.980
she would've kept him hidden longer.

03:58.180 --> 03:59.380
I heard

03:59.820 --> 04:01.460
she signed several authors externally.

04:01.460 --> 04:03.380
Only Gu Yan survived in the end.

04:03.860 --> 04:06.940
The success of one general
is built on the bones of ten thousand.

04:07.220 --> 04:08.060
So,

04:08.133 --> 04:09.180
she probably has backups

04:09.180 --> 04:10.460
for people like us, too.

04:10.660 --> 04:11.420
She can replace us.

04:11.620 --> 04:13.500
I thought our boss was sweet and naive.

04:13.980 --> 04:15.420
But she's just as calculating.

04:17.060 --> 04:19.540
Tense, anxious, and paranoid.

04:23.940 --> 04:25.300
This book, "Oblivious and Unhappy",

04:25.300 --> 04:26.060
is pretty good.

04:26.740 --> 04:27.300
I'll read it.

04:28.140 --> 04:28.620
Ms. Lin.

04:31.100 --> 04:32.380
Why are you covered in sweat?

04:32.900 --> 04:34.700
I took the bus here. I ran a bit,

04:34.700 --> 04:35.700
so I wouldn't be late.

04:35.700 --> 04:36.822
I'll walk you to the junction.

04:36.940 --> 04:37.300
Let's go.

04:42.300 --> 04:42.980
Is that Gu Yan?

04:44.180 --> 04:44.900
I think so.

04:47.580 --> 04:48.100
Do you know

04:48.100 --> 04:49.380
why that guy kept staring at you?

04:50.140 --> 04:50.740
Why?

04:51.780 --> 04:52.660
He also

04:52.900 --> 04:53.500
wrote a draft.

04:53.980 --> 04:54.820
You came out on top.

04:55.260 --> 04:56.180
So he put his pen down.

04:58.300 --> 04:59.340
Thank you,

04:59.860 --> 05:00.820
for this opportunity.

05:01.300 --> 05:02.620
You earned it yourself.

05:02.844 --> 05:04.066
I didn't give it to you.

05:04.300 --> 05:04.866
Right here.

05:08.660 --> 05:09.577
Morning, Ms. Lin.

05:09.622 --> 05:11.100
Cindy, this is Gu Yan.

05:11.180 --> 05:12.120
Please take care of him.

05:12.140 --> 05:13.260
Show him around the office.

05:13.333 --> 05:14.540
Introduce him to everyone.

05:15.066 --> 05:15.740
Will do, Ms. Lin.

05:16.620 --> 05:17.220
Mr. Gu Yan.

05:18.220 --> 05:19.660
Please sign in.

05:35.260 --> 05:35.780
Ms. Lin.

05:37.180 --> 05:37.977
It's all signed?

05:38.420 --> 05:39.700
He barely read it before signing.

05:40.140 --> 05:41.180
He said he wouldn't

05:41.180 --> 05:42.822
let the opportunity slip away this time.

05:44.644 --> 05:45.860
As long as he has that drive.

05:46.980 --> 05:47.420
Ms. Lin.

05:48.060 --> 05:49.260
I have a question...

05:51.020 --> 05:51.380
for you.

05:53.980 --> 05:55.020
Are you going to ask

05:55.340 --> 05:56.060
how many are now

05:56.266 --> 05:57.900
working back-to-back
on each project?

05:59.133 --> 06:00.911
Different projects
are handled differently.

06:01.500 --> 06:02.980
For proposals that are good

06:03.420 --> 06:04.340
and show promise,

06:04.780 --> 06:05.540
I'll assign

06:05.666 --> 06:07.688
several groups
to write them separately.

06:08.300 --> 06:09.980
Isn't that really...

06:10.755 --> 06:13.244
Wouldn't the people
who aren't chosen feel cheated?

06:13.420 --> 06:15.700
I just saw Sanzang
and felt pretty bad for him.

06:15.800 --> 06:17.688
Losing out on skill isn't being cheated.

06:17.900 --> 06:19.660
Then, what about Gu Yan's situation?

06:19.688 --> 06:20.700
Now that it's decided

06:20.700 --> 06:21.820
that he'll continue writing

06:21.820 --> 06:22.620
"Drunk Old Friend",

06:22.688 --> 06:24.800
he'll be the only one
writing it from now on, right?

06:24.900 --> 06:26.300
There won't be any other backups?

06:28.580 --> 06:29.180
Of course not.

06:33.580 --> 06:34.220
That's a relief.

06:34.340 --> 06:35.666
I'd like to introduce everyone

06:35.822 --> 06:36.380
to Gu Yan.

06:43.180 --> 06:44.780
Over the past year or so,

06:45.060 --> 06:47.244
Gu Yan and I
were still getting to know each other.

06:47.580 --> 06:48.300
So, we agreed

06:48.500 --> 06:49.580
to keep things quiet.

06:49.977 --> 06:52.020
We waited until
the first fifty chapters were out

06:52.140 --> 06:53.955
before making
further plans for our collab.

06:54.740 --> 06:56.020
I can now tell you all

06:56.700 --> 06:57.940
that we have actually finished

06:57.940 --> 06:59.180
the first 120 chapters.

07:00.220 --> 07:02.540
And film adaptation rights
are already being negotiated.

07:05.580 --> 07:05.980
Go on.

07:09.820 --> 07:11.060
Although it's my name

07:11.180 --> 07:12.940
on the author line,

07:13.620 --> 07:14.420
the truth is that

07:14.820 --> 07:15.700
most of the credit

07:16.380 --> 07:17.380
goes to Ms. Lin.

07:18.100 --> 07:20.140
I don't have much going on usually.

07:20.711 --> 07:21.580
Except for sleeping,

07:22.700 --> 07:25.180
I spend all my time
writing novels with her.

07:26.288 --> 07:28.260
We have a lot of authors
with good attitudes.

07:28.466 --> 07:29.340
Lawyer Bei is here.

07:29.860 --> 07:32.620
But a top-tier author
with an attitude this good?

07:33.540 --> 07:34.380
You're the first.

07:34.540 --> 07:35.860
- Impressive!
- Absolutely!

07:35.860 --> 07:36.820
Let's give him a hand!

07:36.820 --> 07:38.020
Come on!

07:49.220 --> 07:49.700
Mr. Bei.

07:51.260 --> 07:52.000
This is thick.

07:52.460 --> 07:53.420
Per your request,

07:53.533 --> 07:54.820
I've detailed clauses covering

07:54.980 --> 07:55.955
the partnership duration,

07:55.980 --> 07:56.820
content scope,

07:57.180 --> 07:58.260
copyright confidentiality,

07:58.260 --> 07:59.400
and decision-making power.

07:59.700 --> 08:00.620
Once he gets here,

08:00.980 --> 08:02.060
I'll walk him through it.

08:02.420 --> 08:03.420
You need not be present.

08:03.740 --> 08:04.940
I can handle the negotiations.

08:06.460 --> 08:07.380
Okay, thanks.

08:10.420 --> 08:10.820
Gu Yan.

08:11.100 --> 08:12.780
Wait in Ms. Lin's office for a bit.

08:15.100 --> 08:16.940
She's having a quick word with Mr. Bei.

08:17.060 --> 08:18.180
She'll call you in later.

08:19.860 --> 08:20.180
Water.

08:26.780 --> 08:28.300
Since we have a minute,

08:28.300 --> 08:30.140
I want to confirm a few things with you.

08:30.420 --> 08:31.700
Your home address

08:31.700 --> 08:33.180
and your daily schedule.

08:36.266 --> 08:37.540
We'll add each other on WeChat.

08:37.600 --> 08:38.977
If I need to chase you for drafts

08:39.000 --> 08:39.740
or if the company...

08:39.740 --> 08:40.180
No need.

08:42.340 --> 08:43.620
What do you mean?

08:45.020 --> 08:46.666
I'll just contact Ms. Lin directly.

08:49.260 --> 08:50.700
Let me reintroduce myself.

08:50.820 --> 08:52.580
Cai Zhangzhu, Lin Zhanqiao's assistant.

08:53.100 --> 08:54.180
Part of my job

08:54.180 --> 08:56.060
is maintaining
her relationships with authors.

08:56.540 --> 08:57.140
She's busy.

08:57.660 --> 08:59.460
I handle
all the trivial stuff for her first.

08:59.660 --> 09:01.820
Ms. Lin handles my affairs directly.

09:04.980 --> 09:06.660
Why are you so two-faced?

09:06.755 --> 09:08.300
You're all nice in front of Ms. Lin.

09:08.540 --> 09:10.266
When she's gone, you're just arrogant.

09:14.460 --> 09:15.700
I only talk to Lin Zhanqiao.

09:19.180 --> 09:19.540
Gu Yan.

09:20.500 --> 09:21.140
Come in.

09:38.260 --> 09:39.580
We'll probably need to chat

09:39.900 --> 09:41.300
for up to an hour and a half.

09:42.500 --> 09:44.300
Ms. Lin, if you're busy,
you can go ahead.

09:45.140 --> 09:45.460
Alright.

09:45.900 --> 09:47.060
Have you read these contracts?

09:47.700 --> 09:48.420
I have.

09:48.740 --> 09:50.340
If you have, I'll just sign them.

09:51.020 --> 09:52.340
You should let Mr. Bei

09:52.340 --> 09:53.500
give you a quick rundown.

09:54.140 --> 09:55.260
If there are any clauses

09:55.540 --> 09:56.860
you feel aren't quite right,

09:57.180 --> 09:58.300
we can still negotiate.

09:58.620 --> 09:59.020
No need.

10:01.620 --> 10:03.500
First off, you need to know

10:04.020 --> 10:06.820
that your contract with Chenxing Culture
has been extended

10:07.460 --> 10:08.580
from five years to eight.

10:09.900 --> 10:10.380
No problem.

10:12.460 --> 10:12.860
Second...

10:13.066 --> 10:14.177
I just sign here, right?

10:15.500 --> 10:15.820
Here.

10:17.700 --> 10:18.060
Yes.

10:45.660 --> 10:47.540
(Gu Yan's blind trust in me)

10:47.940 --> 10:48.700
(is touching,)

10:49.420 --> 10:50.980
(but it also makes me uneasy.)

10:52.340 --> 10:53.700
(If He Han's issue was)

10:53.980 --> 10:55.500
(a lack of commitment,)

10:56.044 --> 10:58.060
(then the pressure Gu Yan
is putting on me now)

10:58.900 --> 11:00.420
(is an unbearable weight.)

11:02.620 --> 11:03.140
Ms. Lin.

11:04.622 --> 11:06.260
Gu Yan refuses to give me his WeChat

11:06.380 --> 11:07.460
or any contact info.

11:07.900 --> 11:09.066
I'll talk to him about it.

11:09.380 --> 11:10.660
He's probably just shy.

11:10.980 --> 11:12.940
No, what I mean is,
I'll do whatever it takes

11:12.940 --> 11:14.180
to make him communicate with me.

11:14.500 --> 11:15.380
I'll handle him.

11:16.700 --> 11:17.220
Good.

11:18.900 --> 11:20.380
One more thing to report.

11:21.020 --> 11:22.540
Mimi started a new series.

11:24.540 --> 11:25.300
"Cherish Life,

11:25.380 --> 11:26.250
Stay Away From Jerks."

11:26.260 --> 11:26.860
Oh, you knew?

11:30.100 --> 11:30.940
Isn't this

11:30.940 --> 11:31.820
par for the course

11:31.820 --> 11:32.780
for all his girlfriends?

11:33.740 --> 11:35.020
When they're madly in love,

11:35.180 --> 11:36.577
they write "The CEO Fell For Me."

11:37.260 --> 11:38.300
When they break up,

11:38.740 --> 11:40.044
they write "The Jerk Chronicles."

11:41.820 --> 11:42.300
You read it?

11:42.540 --> 11:42.860
I...

11:43.500 --> 11:44.860
I took a quick look.

11:45.100 --> 11:47.380
Honestly, it's pretty vividly written.

11:49.180 --> 11:50.355
It speaks from her heart.

11:54.140 --> 11:54.740
All done.

11:56.020 --> 11:56.500
Thanks.

11:58.380 --> 11:59.460
Zhangzhu will walk you down.

11:59.740 --> 12:00.100
Okay.

12:08.220 --> 12:09.420
I'm so sorry, Mr. Bei.

12:09.820 --> 12:12.020
I dragged you
all the way here for nothing.

12:13.940 --> 12:16.220
I really thought I'd have to
spend ages convincing him.

12:16.220 --> 12:18.260
Who knew I'd be done in a few minutes?

12:19.300 --> 12:20.020
To be honest,

12:20.860 --> 12:21.860
his trust in me

12:22.380 --> 12:24.580
is both encouraging and stressful.

12:25.933 --> 12:27.940
That's exactly
what I wanted to warn you about.

12:28.260 --> 12:29.220
You need to be careful.

12:39.244 --> 12:41.022
Has anyone ever called you two-faced?

12:46.460 --> 12:48.420
Authors with bad attitudes
never last long.

12:48.540 --> 12:49.100
You know that?

12:49.620 --> 12:50.380
Like He Han?

13:14.180 --> 13:15.820
When was the last time
you got to rest?

13:16.660 --> 13:17.700
No one is bothering you.

13:18.060 --> 13:18.940
No meetings.

13:19.220 --> 13:20.300
No deadlines.

13:20.460 --> 13:22.340
No calls, no interviews.

13:22.660 --> 13:24.700
I bet you barely have
any WeChat messages either.

13:25.300 --> 13:26.500
Pretty comfortable, right?

13:26.660 --> 13:27.620
Yeah, it is.

13:27.620 --> 13:28.940
It will stay that way for a while.

13:29.100 --> 13:31.220
Because all the editors
are chasing Gu Yan now.

13:32.177 --> 13:33.500
You finally have some free time.

13:33.500 --> 13:36.020
Why don't you take a few days off?

13:36.020 --> 13:37.130
Go out and have some fun.

13:37.130 --> 13:37.700
I will.

13:38.740 --> 13:40.500
But I'm worried that when I get back,

13:40.500 --> 13:42.060
I'll have to hand you my resignation.

13:42.220 --> 13:43.260
It won't come to that.

13:43.260 --> 13:44.644
Go on, go wherever you want.

13:44.666 --> 13:46.260
Food, drinks, entertainment, travel,

13:46.260 --> 13:47.140
I'll cover it all.

13:48.660 --> 13:49.420
For the next week,

13:49.420 --> 13:50.620
I'm not going anywhere.

13:50.700 --> 13:53.540
I'm just going to stay right here
and watch you waste time.

13:53.540 --> 13:54.860
I'm not wasting time.

13:54.860 --> 13:56.500
Don't you know authors need rest?

13:56.500 --> 13:57.660
We need time to reflect,

13:57.660 --> 13:58.980
and to experience life.

13:59.644 --> 14:02.177
Here are the questions
for this afternoon's interview.

14:02.420 --> 14:03.540
See?

14:03.780 --> 14:05.100
Someone is bothering me now.

14:06.020 --> 14:08.340
Take a good look
at these questions first.

14:08.340 --> 14:10.700
They're all about Gu Yan.

14:11.820 --> 14:12.860
The last two aren't.

14:13.300 --> 14:14.700
One asks if I'm still writing,

14:14.900 --> 14:16.888
and the other asks
if I have a new girlfriend.

14:18.660 --> 14:19.260
He Han.

14:21.620 --> 14:23.500
I can cancel this interview for you.

14:24.620 --> 14:25.220
Don't do that.

14:25.288 --> 14:27.822
If you do it,
then I'll have no one bothering me.

14:32.620 --> 14:34.940
Then, don't mention
that you've met Gu Yan.

14:35.780 --> 14:37.380
People will think
you're fixated on him.

14:41.420 --> 14:42.500
Hello, Mr. He Han.

14:42.700 --> 14:43.500
Have you noticed

14:43.500 --> 14:46.180
the new author, Gu Yan,
who's exploded onto the scene recently?

14:46.420 --> 14:47.060
Of course.

14:47.300 --> 14:49.155
I haven't just noticed him,
and I've met him.

14:49.300 --> 14:51.860
Don't say you've read
"Drunk Old Friend".

14:52.460 --> 14:53.260
Don't comment on it.

14:53.620 --> 14:55.260
Whether you praise it or criticize it,

14:55.511 --> 14:56.644
it'll cause problems.

14:56.980 --> 14:58.500
Have you read Gu Yan's novel?

14:58.700 --> 15:00.380
I have. "Drunk Old Friend", right?

15:00.900 --> 15:03.220
And what are your thoughts on it?

15:03.660 --> 15:04.300
It's nice.

15:06.220 --> 15:07.540
But it might end badly.

15:10.133 --> 15:10.740
Can he really

15:10.740 --> 15:12.177
say that in front of so many people?

15:13.020 --> 15:13.660
Isn't this

15:13.660 --> 15:14.900
why he agreed to this interview?

15:14.977 --> 15:16.180
I don't care about that stuff.

15:16.260 --> 15:18.222
Whatever I write,
people will read it anyway.

15:22.500 --> 15:23.940
Look how smug he is.

15:25.244 --> 15:26.420
Will it have a bad ending?

15:27.700 --> 15:28.700
You actually believe him?

15:31.340 --> 15:33.020
I don't trust him on other things,

15:33.540 --> 15:35.020
but when it comes to writing novels,

15:35.620 --> 15:36.740
I actually trust him a bit.

15:38.260 --> 15:39.380
He's jealous of Gu Yan.

15:39.980 --> 15:41.220
He'll crash and burn first.

15:43.100 --> 15:44.200
Just another half a month.

15:44.580 --> 15:45.511
When he starts writing

15:45.860 --> 15:47.380
and goes head-to-head with Gu Yan,

15:47.700 --> 15:48.860
he won't be so smug then.

15:54.100 --> 15:54.900
A bad ending?

15:56.400 --> 15:58.180
I doubt he'll even
make it to the ending.

15:59.940 --> 16:02.288
Does it give you a thrill
to go around spreading rumors?

16:02.780 --> 16:04.620
Making baseless claims like that

16:04.620 --> 16:06.740
just makes you look cheap!

16:08.755 --> 16:10.180
You don't care about Gu Yan, fine.

16:10.340 --> 16:11.577
If you offend him, whatever.

16:11.580 --> 16:12.540
But what about Dingqi?

16:12.660 --> 16:13.500
You're saying

16:13.500 --> 16:15.740
their number-one novel is going to flop?

16:15.820 --> 16:16.340
What?

16:16.540 --> 16:17.460
Do you not plan

16:17.460 --> 16:18.660
on working with Dingqi?

16:19.980 --> 16:21.140
I'm telling the truth!

16:21.420 --> 16:22.580
I'm just worried about them.

16:22.580 --> 16:23.540
I gave them a heads-up.

16:27.700 --> 16:28.244
Come here.

16:28.500 --> 16:30.540
I've got my phone on 0.5x speed.

16:30.540 --> 16:31.780
I'll play it back for you.

16:31.980 --> 16:33.980
If you can find even a shred

16:33.980 --> 16:35.340
of genuine concern in your voice,

16:35.700 --> 16:36.580
I'll eat my phone.

16:37.980 --> 16:38.420
No...

16:38.820 --> 16:40.780
I'm really doing Dingqi a favor here.

16:40.900 --> 16:41.620
Think about it.

16:41.940 --> 16:43.740
If I say
this great novel is going to flop,

16:43.740 --> 16:45.020
won't everyone flock to read it

16:45.020 --> 16:46.460
just to see when it falls apart?

16:46.820 --> 16:48.100
That's all clicks.

16:48.100 --> 16:49.700
You're a good writer,

16:49.700 --> 16:50.560
so you can be a jerk.

16:50.580 --> 16:51.980
But you can't do nothing

16:51.980 --> 16:53.060
and still act like a jerk!

16:59.820 --> 17:00.460
He Han!

17:01.060 --> 17:02.460
Open up. It's Mimi!

17:03.460 --> 17:04.290
How did she get here?

17:04.290 --> 17:05.700
How should I know?

17:06.540 --> 17:07.300
Why is she here?

17:08.180 --> 17:08.740
He Han!

17:09.060 --> 17:11.180
I brought your favorite
Drunken Chicken Hot Pot!

17:12.260 --> 17:13.980
Can we just talk?

17:14.540 --> 17:16.020
Since when do I like Drunken Chicken?

17:16.380 --> 17:17.460
Handle it. I'm not here.

17:32.260 --> 17:32.900
Where's He Han?

17:33.900 --> 17:34.500
He's not here.

17:34.980 --> 17:36.111
How did you get up here?

17:36.380 --> 17:37.300
I'm calling security.

17:38.300 --> 17:39.340
I booked a room

17:39.340 --> 17:40.300
on the 31st floor.

17:40.460 --> 17:41.444
Right across from his.

17:42.088 --> 17:43.540
Calling security won't do any good.

17:45.460 --> 17:46.180
What do you want?

17:48.020 --> 17:49.200
I want to apologize to him.

17:50.020 --> 17:51.380
He did so much for me.

17:52.140 --> 17:53.060
And I humiliated him.

17:53.620 --> 17:54.980
I want to apologize in person.

17:55.500 --> 17:56.977
I want us to get back together.

17:57.020 --> 17:58.380
No thanks, spare me.

18:01.060 --> 18:01.940
He has a girlfriend.

18:03.900 --> 18:04.780
Impossible.

18:05.900 --> 18:06.500
We broke up

18:06.500 --> 18:07.900
less than forty-eight hours ago.

18:08.540 --> 18:09.060
He Han?

18:09.540 --> 18:11.660
You think that's hard for him?

18:13.900 --> 18:14.500
He Han!

18:16.260 --> 18:16.780
He Han!

18:17.220 --> 18:17.860
He Han!

18:18.740 --> 18:19.820
I know you're in there!

18:21.180 --> 18:21.860
He Han!

18:24.220 --> 18:24.820
He Han!

18:28.900 --> 18:29.540
He Han!

18:34.300 --> 18:35.060
He's not here.

18:35.260 --> 18:35.900
Just go.

18:36.980 --> 18:38.340
Take your drunken chicken,

18:38.540 --> 18:41.140
and go back
to writing your "Wide Awake".

18:50.700 --> 18:53.260
(Mengtong Internet Cafe)

18:53.260 --> 18:54.380
♪Never stop♪

18:57.577 --> 18:58.540
Here's your delivery.

18:58.540 --> 18:59.488
Leave a five-star rating.

18:59.500 --> 19:00.260
Okay, thanks.

19:01.340 --> 19:01.820
Er Jiu.

19:02.620 --> 19:03.220
Food's here.

19:04.020 --> 19:05.060
♪Never stop♪

19:06.260 --> 19:07.420
Whoa, already?

19:08.340 --> 19:09.540
I swear we just ordered.

19:10.260 --> 19:10.740
Hurry.

19:11.400 --> 19:12.260
Give me a hand.

19:12.340 --> 19:13.060
Almost done.

19:13.540 --> 19:14.300
Help me out here!

19:14.400 --> 19:15.140
I'm almost done!

19:16.466 --> 19:17.140
It's all greasy.

19:18.177 --> 19:19.540
Why is it leaking so much grease?

19:19.550 --> 19:20.220
Get some napkins.

19:20.300 --> 19:21.020
Alright.

19:23.180 --> 19:24.380
No, you keep playing.

19:27.060 --> 19:29.140
So now that you're making money writing,

19:29.311 --> 19:30.970
you can just
boss your girlfriend around?

19:31.980 --> 19:34.140
You just never stop
mentioning the girlfriend.

19:34.540 --> 19:35.580
Do you even have one?

19:36.622 --> 19:38.260
Why do you care if I have a girlfriend?

19:38.511 --> 19:40.580
I'm just saying,
don't forget where you came from.

19:40.900 --> 19:41.620
And where is that?

19:42.500 --> 19:44.020
Beating you up, that's where! Log in.

19:44.180 --> 19:45.400
Let me finish eating first.

19:45.780 --> 19:46.180
Napkins.

19:47.300 --> 19:48.220
♪Never stop♪

19:48.733 --> 19:49.577
Eat this.

19:49.688 --> 19:51.300
When you're done,
help me with the Cangwu raid.

19:51.300 --> 19:51.780
Got it?

19:51.860 --> 19:53.300
Cangwu is child's play.

19:53.822 --> 19:56.133
I'll even carry you
through the Snowy Cave today.

19:56.688 --> 19:57.933
I'm taking another piece.

19:58.000 --> 19:59.060
♪Never stop♪

19:59.060 --> 20:00.088
♪From the sea of stars♪

20:00.977 --> 20:01.740
Wait, seriously?

20:02.666 --> 20:03.420
They're all gone?

20:03.711 --> 20:04.540
Only four pieces.

20:04.980 --> 20:05.620
Only four?

20:05.620 --> 20:06.940
Why did he eat two?

20:07.820 --> 20:08.900
Why do you eat so much?

20:08.980 --> 20:09.940
Stop bickering.

20:09.940 --> 20:11.220
I'll just order more.

20:11.933 --> 20:13.540
Look at you, acting like a big shot.

20:13.940 --> 20:14.740
It's annoying.

20:15.888 --> 20:17.060
Ms. Lin is looking for me.

20:17.377 --> 20:18.460
I'm going to meet her.

20:19.400 --> 20:21.140
Didn't you just say
we're doing the raid?

20:21.140 --> 20:22.200
Now it's back to Ms. Lin?

20:22.580 --> 20:23.580
I must talk to her.

20:23.844 --> 20:24.620
When we're done,

20:24.980 --> 20:25.860
I'll help you out.

20:30.500 --> 20:31.340
Sit down and eat.

20:34.820 --> 20:35.380
Forget it.

20:42.300 --> 20:43.300
This was long overdue.

20:43.600 --> 20:44.340
Congratulations on

20:44.500 --> 20:45.140
your success.

20:45.700 --> 20:46.100
Thanks.

20:46.380 --> 20:47.820
Actually, congrats to both of us.

20:48.580 --> 20:49.340
I brought food.

20:50.300 --> 20:51.540
Is this just for me,

20:51.700 --> 20:52.580
or both of us?

20:52.580 --> 20:53.410
I haven't eaten yet.

20:53.420 --> 20:54.288
Talk while you eat.

20:54.780 --> 20:55.266
Come on.

21:03.420 --> 21:03.700
Here.

21:11.740 --> 21:12.300
So, tell me.

21:12.460 --> 21:13.380
How did it feel

21:13.580 --> 21:14.180
to go public?

21:15.460 --> 21:16.460
I was a little nervous.

21:18.060 --> 21:19.020
But it wasn't so bad

21:19.333 --> 21:20.177
with you there.

21:22.380 --> 21:23.140
I just knew

21:23.911 --> 21:25.466
that no matter what happened,

21:26.555 --> 21:27.340
if I left it to you,

21:27.620 --> 21:28.500
you'd figure it out.

21:29.660 --> 21:31.820
But you need to learn
to face your readers yourself.

21:32.600 --> 21:34.340
You have to learn
how to engage with them,

21:34.666 --> 21:35.540
answering comments,

21:35.820 --> 21:36.800
and rallying support.

21:38.540 --> 21:39.100
A web novelist

21:39.100 --> 21:40.660
needs some social skills.

21:41.500 --> 21:42.380
Many web novelists

21:42.380 --> 21:43.820
build their own fan circles.

21:44.140 --> 21:45.540
It helps you connect with readers

21:45.860 --> 21:47.260
and show them you're genuine.

21:47.700 --> 21:48.940
Then, they'll start promoting

21:48.940 --> 21:50.580
your work across every platform.

21:51.155 --> 21:52.333
Can you do it for me?

21:52.420 --> 21:53.340
I'm not good at that.

21:54.220 --> 21:54.860
I can teach you.

21:55.940 --> 21:56.660
Can you learn?

21:58.020 --> 21:59.140
I just want to write.

22:01.260 --> 22:02.777
You're a rare breed, you know that?

22:03.460 --> 22:04.500
Most authors would die

22:04.500 --> 22:05.780
to be independent fast.

22:06.340 --> 22:06.740
That way,

22:06.740 --> 22:08.210
you have more leverage

22:08.210 --> 22:09.622
when negotiating terms later on.

22:11.180 --> 22:11.740
I only have

22:12.500 --> 22:13.380
one condition.

22:14.580 --> 22:15.820
Keep writing by my side.

22:17.820 --> 22:18.420
No problem.

22:18.577 --> 22:19.666
I can promise you that.

22:21.660 --> 22:22.100
Who is it?

22:23.220 --> 22:23.620
It's me.

22:25.180 --> 22:25.580
Coming!

22:29.380 --> 22:30.133
Why are you here?

22:32.180 --> 22:33.220
I brought some fruit

22:33.220 --> 22:34.180
for you guys.

22:34.260 --> 22:34.860
It's washed.

22:34.860 --> 22:36.100
You can snack while you talk.

22:36.380 --> 22:37.860
Perfect timing. Join us for a drink.

22:40.860 --> 22:42.100
Didn't you just eat?

22:46.460 --> 22:47.860
Quick, pour San Mei a glass.

22:49.260 --> 22:51.020
Better let Ms. Zhanqiao handle that.

22:51.180 --> 22:52.460
We wanted to open a bottle,

22:52.460 --> 22:53.100
but he refused.

22:53.580 --> 22:54.380
I'm his boss.

22:54.460 --> 22:55.755
He's too polite to say no to me.

22:56.180 --> 22:57.980
I'm not big on celebrations.

22:58.180 --> 22:58.980
You know that.

22:59.980 --> 23:00.300
Here.

23:07.340 --> 23:08.340
Hand me a cup.

23:08.580 --> 23:09.860
I'll bring some up for Er Jiu.

23:17.220 --> 23:18.420
Enjoy your food.

23:18.540 --> 23:19.220
I'm heading out.

23:21.555 --> 23:23.088
Don't forget to help me with the raid.

23:23.500 --> 23:24.380
I got it.

23:42.800 --> 23:45.060
San Mei gets anxious
whenever you change even a little.

23:45.780 --> 23:46.911
No matter how much I change,

23:47.100 --> 23:48.755
it's not like I'm leaving this place.

23:49.820 --> 23:50.780
Not the internet cafe.

23:50.780 --> 23:52.044
I'm talking about San Mei.

23:58.380 --> 24:00.660
(This is so exciting. I love it!)

24:00.660 --> 24:01.580
(Gu Yan has a bright future.)
Wait, is Wang Hai

24:01.580 --> 24:03.180
(So young and such a good writer!)
going to have a fan base?

24:03.940 --> 24:04.940
No need to wait.

24:05.380 --> 24:06.380
He's already got one.

24:09.980 --> 24:11.020
What's wrong? Worried?

24:11.340 --> 24:12.260
Worrying won't help.

24:12.700 --> 24:13.580
There are always others.

24:14.444 --> 24:16.220
You can't tell whether
a fan is male or female

24:16.220 --> 24:17.260
from their online username.

24:17.540 --> 24:19.180
The fans are definitely a mix of both.

24:24.955 --> 24:26.020
The ones who tip a lot

24:26.020 --> 24:27.340
must be loaded, right?

24:28.580 --> 24:30.660
I've heard of authors hitting it big

24:30.660 --> 24:32.022
and ending up with their fans.

24:33.060 --> 24:34.380
Like that guy, Ge Zhong Jian.

24:35.380 --> 24:36.460
Ge Zhong Jian's wife

24:36.540 --> 24:38.180
is prettier than a movie star.

24:48.060 --> 24:48.780
But San Mei,

24:48.940 --> 24:49.540
honestly,

24:49.844 --> 24:52.060
if you dressed up,
you'd be prettier than any star.

24:53.820 --> 24:54.660
No, thanks.

24:55.020 --> 24:56.700
I like being myself.

24:57.200 --> 24:58.620
If he changes his persona every day,

24:58.620 --> 24:59.660
am I supposed to keep up?

24:59.860 --> 25:01.180
Who's going to look after my cafe?

25:02.900 --> 25:04.420
What's the toughest part about you?

25:05.180 --> 25:05.580
The mouth.

25:06.660 --> 25:07.020
Get lost!

25:08.311 --> 25:08.980
Struck a nerve,

25:09.540 --> 25:10.220
didn't I?

25:12.140 --> 25:13.260
What's great about this wine?

25:13.940 --> 25:14.660
Beer's way better.

25:28.700 --> 25:29.060
Okay.

25:50.420 --> 25:51.180
What's in the bag?

25:59.980 --> 26:01.140
Mustard mushroom crisps.

26:01.980 --> 26:03.620
Flavors used to be subtle.

26:04.260 --> 26:05.220
Now, they are intense.

26:06.100 --> 26:07.340
Everyone's chasing a rush.

26:08.100 --> 26:10.260
Without that kick,
there's no market for it.

26:15.380 --> 26:15.900
Want some?

26:17.060 --> 26:17.620
No way.

26:17.933 --> 26:18.660
I'm not drinking.

26:18.820 --> 26:19.380
Absolutely not.

26:20.180 --> 26:21.220
I'm just testing you

26:21.220 --> 26:22.300
to check your resolve.

26:23.580 --> 26:24.380
On this street,

26:24.380 --> 26:26.180
no one has more resolve than me.

26:26.740 --> 26:27.580
I'm the most solid.

26:29.380 --> 26:30.970
You never thought about sneaking a sip?

26:30.970 --> 26:32.100
No one would know.

26:33.500 --> 26:34.060
Never.

26:35.180 --> 26:36.622
You'll get it when you've felt it.

26:37.460 --> 26:38.220
Sometimes,

26:38.420 --> 26:39.420
your obsessions

26:39.540 --> 26:40.820
and the ones you'd die for

26:41.140 --> 26:42.260
will be gone for good

26:42.940 --> 26:44.140
once you let go.

26:45.020 --> 26:45.820
And other times,

26:46.340 --> 26:47.860
the stuff you thought didn't matter

26:48.100 --> 26:48.900
starts haunting you

26:48.900 --> 26:51.220
once it's actually gone.

26:54.860 --> 26:55.540
I hope

26:55.540 --> 26:57.180
I never have to
find out what it's like.

28:00.660 --> 28:01.740
Mr. He Han.

28:01.980 --> 28:02.888
Where's your boss?

28:03.940 --> 28:04.780
She's already off.

28:10.140 --> 28:10.540
And you?

28:10.900 --> 28:11.580
Still working?

28:12.740 --> 28:14.420
I still have some work to finish.

28:15.020 --> 28:16.380
What work keeps you this late?

28:17.020 --> 28:19.170
She's making a rookie
like you work overtime.

28:19.170 --> 28:20.300
Lin Zhanqiao is too much.

28:21.700 --> 28:22.380
Just head home.

28:22.500 --> 28:23.222
Do you live far?

28:23.860 --> 28:25.220
It's alright.

28:26.300 --> 28:27.555
I'm not offering you a ride.

28:28.100 --> 28:29.540
I'm just saying, if you live far,

28:29.540 --> 28:30.700
be careful taking a cab.

28:30.980 --> 28:32.180
Use the phone's safety feature.

28:32.288 --> 28:34.088
Set Lin Zhanqiao
as your emergency contact.

28:34.090 --> 28:36.000
She's making you stay late,
so she's responsible.

28:36.580 --> 28:37.700
She didn't make me stay.

28:37.700 --> 28:38.620
I chose to work late.

28:38.620 --> 28:39.580
Don't defend her.

28:39.580 --> 28:40.500
If a boss is unfair,

28:40.500 --> 28:41.580
you can push back.

28:41.820 --> 28:43.180
Who actually wants to work late?

28:43.380 --> 28:44.700
Wouldn't you rather sleep or read?

28:44.700 --> 28:45.340
No, really.

28:45.620 --> 28:47.300
I'm honestly
just the type who works late.

28:49.020 --> 28:50.810
Ambition is great, girl,

28:50.810 --> 28:52.022
but this isn't the smart way.

28:52.220 --> 28:53.820
It's not about ambition.

28:54.540 --> 28:55.180
What's it about?

28:56.820 --> 28:58.380
I just don't want to go home.

29:00.260 --> 29:00.980
Trouble at home?

29:01.820 --> 29:02.511
More or less.

29:03.600 --> 29:04.866
Good luck with that.

29:12.980 --> 29:14.140
Hey, don't come back yet.

29:15.380 --> 29:17.300
Mimi got a room
right across from yours.

29:17.300 --> 29:19.100
She's sitting
outside your door waiting.

29:39.740 --> 29:40.580
I'm suddenly free.

29:40.800 --> 29:42.900
If you feel like talking
about your home situation,

29:43.180 --> 29:44.300
I can stick around for a bit.

29:55.980 --> 29:57.100
My dad is getting remarried.

29:58.860 --> 30:00.740
He's moving
my stepmother in to live with me.

30:01.220 --> 30:01.820
I hate it.

30:02.180 --> 30:03.340
Hate that he's remarrying,

30:04.220 --> 30:05.822
or just that you have to live with her?

30:07.700 --> 30:08.620
Both.

30:09.300 --> 30:10.260
When my dad

30:10.355 --> 30:12.020
picks a wife,
he only cares about looks,

30:12.020 --> 30:12.860
not about substance.

30:15.700 --> 30:16.460
I can tell.

30:17.980 --> 30:18.740
How can you tell?

30:18.820 --> 30:19.380
Your mom

30:19.380 --> 30:20.940
must have been quite a beauty.

30:30.900 --> 30:32.140
My mom passed away.

30:35.020 --> 30:35.580
I'm so sorry.

30:37.180 --> 30:37.660
It's okay.

30:38.220 --> 30:39.740
She really was beautiful.

30:39.940 --> 30:41.060
But she was a natural beauty.

30:41.222 --> 30:42.620
I'm not sure about this new woman.

30:45.100 --> 30:46.220
Stop calling her "stepmother."

30:46.500 --> 30:47.860
It's 2024.

30:47.940 --> 30:49.740
This isn't Snow White or Cinderella.

30:49.933 --> 30:51.688
Your dad's new wife
is just his new wife.

30:51.733 --> 30:52.960
She has nothing to do with you.

30:52.980 --> 30:54.420
Stepmom, second mom, or whatever...

30:54.580 --> 30:56.100
Your own mother is irreplaceable.

30:56.180 --> 30:56.700
Right?

30:56.820 --> 30:58.660
You can't stop him
from getting married,

30:58.820 --> 30:59.820
but that's his business.

31:00.300 --> 31:01.660
You can certainly set boundaries.

31:02.180 --> 31:03.380
So, you're on my side?

31:03.540 --> 31:04.780
Let me finish.

31:06.100 --> 31:06.620
Look.

31:08.420 --> 31:09.660
Who bought your house?

31:11.820 --> 31:12.300
My dad.

31:13.020 --> 31:13.900
He's a contractor.

31:14.000 --> 31:14.660
He builds houses.

31:14.660 --> 31:15.180
He's loaded.

31:15.180 --> 31:15.620
Exactly.

31:15.780 --> 31:17.100
The house belongs to him.

31:17.300 --> 31:18.660
He's the master of that home.

31:18.860 --> 31:20.420
He has the right to let someone move in.

31:20.540 --> 31:21.688
But you have a choice, too.

31:21.940 --> 31:22.900
You're an adult now.

31:23.180 --> 31:24.580
You can choose to leave.

31:28.100 --> 31:29.610
I have no money, no house.

31:29.610 --> 31:30.300
Then you know

31:30.300 --> 31:31.940
what your goal is from here on out.

31:31.940 --> 31:32.820
Make some money.

31:32.900 --> 31:34.140
Rent a place and move out.

31:34.260 --> 31:35.420
Until then, you'll live under

31:35.420 --> 31:36.460
someone else's roof.

31:36.460 --> 31:37.060
No choice.

31:37.311 --> 31:38.460
Everyone goes through it.

31:38.460 --> 31:39.620
We spend years fighting

31:39.620 --> 31:40.980
just to gain that independence.

31:41.140 --> 31:42.580
But remember one thing.

31:43.460 --> 31:44.820
Do it on your own terms.

31:44.940 --> 31:46.066
Don't rely on anyone.

31:46.540 --> 31:47.420
You're pretty enough

31:47.420 --> 31:48.844
that you could marry into a house.

31:49.020 --> 31:50.140
Don't laugh. I'm serious.

31:51.500 --> 31:52.860
But then it's someone else's house,

31:53.740 --> 31:54.610
not yours.

31:54.610 --> 31:56.220
If they ever want you out,

31:56.220 --> 31:56.780
what then?

31:57.220 --> 31:57.980
Squat there?

31:58.180 --> 31:59.020
Sue them?

31:59.540 --> 32:00.220
It gets ugly.

32:04.540 --> 32:05.820
I'll talk with my dad.

32:05.955 --> 32:07.220
Don't tell him it was my idea.

32:07.980 --> 32:08.500
Why not?

32:09.244 --> 32:10.500
Tell him it came from your boss.

32:12.666 --> 32:13.420
Aren't you leaving?

32:13.500 --> 32:14.740
I'll stay a bit longer. Go home.

32:15.140 --> 32:16.020
I'll lock the door.

32:20.300 --> 32:22.250
Don't worry.
There are cameras everywhere.

32:22.250 --> 32:23.050
I'm a public figure.

32:23.050 --> 32:24.380
I have an image to maintain.

32:47.660 --> 32:48.380
Ready?

32:49.140 --> 32:50.340
We're about to tackle

32:50.340 --> 32:51.844
the hardest part of the story so far.

32:54.820 --> 32:56.060
The route we took previously

32:56.580 --> 32:57.580
bypassed Guazhou and

32:58.140 --> 32:59.300
went straight to Zhichi Gorge,

32:59.580 --> 33:00.580
reaching Zhegutian.

33:02.940 --> 33:04.740
Guazhou was mentioned constantly,

33:05.140 --> 33:06.900
yet the story just skipped over it.

33:07.380 --> 33:08.620
That never made sense to me.

33:10.220 --> 33:11.660
You and He Han mapped out

33:11.660 --> 33:13.088
the outline and the route together.

33:13.340 --> 33:13.860
Why did you

33:14.140 --> 33:15.500
bypass Guazhou back then?

33:18.700 --> 33:20.300
Because the plot was stolen.

33:29.260 --> 33:32.220
(2019)

33:43.540 --> 33:44.100
What's wrong?

33:44.500 --> 33:45.020
Read it.

33:45.660 --> 33:46.260
What is this?

33:52.980 --> 33:53.260
Wait...

33:54.340 --> 33:55.140
Who wrote this?

33:55.140 --> 33:56.780
Looks familiar, doesn't it?

33:57.460 --> 33:57.940
Exactly.

33:57.940 --> 33:59.300
That's your Guazhou storyline.

33:59.555 --> 34:01.700
Someone rebranded it
and passed it off as their own!

34:01.720 --> 34:02.820
You're still on the outline,

34:02.820 --> 34:04.420
but they've published the full text.

34:04.700 --> 34:05.980
Who wrote this?

34:05.980 --> 34:07.340
How should I know?

34:07.500 --> 34:08.460
I was going to ask you.

34:09.340 --> 34:10.730
Who did you tell about this?

34:10.730 --> 34:11.620
No one.

34:11.820 --> 34:12.540
That's impossible.

34:16.020 --> 34:17.500
How did it leak?

34:22.060 --> 34:23.180
Someone must have

34:23.866 --> 34:25.511
snapped a photo of the draft.

34:26.740 --> 34:27.820
So we decided

34:28.580 --> 34:29.980
to design a completely new route.

34:31.340 --> 34:36.340
(Zhichi Gorge)

34:50.860 --> 34:52.700
Let's hold off on writing
until I've figured out

34:53.340 --> 34:54.020
how to rewrite

34:54.260 --> 34:54.980
the Guazhou arc.

34:59.260 --> 35:00.980
In a million-word novel,

35:02.940 --> 35:04.980
not every single chapter
has to be perfect

35:05.900 --> 35:07.420
before it reaches the readers.

35:12.500 --> 35:13.300
I disagree.

35:19.060 --> 35:20.780
So we moved on to the Zhichi Gorge.

35:21.700 --> 35:22.580
We followed that plan,

35:22.980 --> 35:24.220
only to realize afterward

35:24.860 --> 35:27.266
it wasn't nearly as good
as the original Guazhou arc.

35:28.500 --> 35:30.260
Is that why

35:30.740 --> 35:31.460
Drunk Old Friend

35:31.460 --> 35:32.380
was never finished?

35:33.420 --> 35:33.740
Yes.

35:34.580 --> 35:35.700
He insisted on finding a way

35:35.700 --> 35:37.660
to top the original Guazhou arc

35:37.777 --> 35:38.955
before he'd start writing.

35:39.540 --> 35:40.340
But he never did?

35:40.740 --> 35:41.100
Never.

35:43.740 --> 35:44.260
Let's do it.

35:44.733 --> 35:45.700
Take the Guazhou route.

35:46.380 --> 35:48.020
He Han couldn't do it, but maybe we can.

35:49.700 --> 35:51.060
But you don't have much time.

35:51.580 --> 35:52.780
You have three days at most.

35:53.180 --> 35:54.260
If you haven't

35:54.380 --> 35:55.700
figured it out by then,

35:56.220 --> 35:57.180
you'll miss the update.

35:57.540 --> 35:58.340
I want to try.

35:59.060 --> 36:00.660
I want to prove I'm better than He Han.

36:05.780 --> 36:07.100
Is the lore book still around?

36:10.400 --> 36:11.511
I'll ask He Han for it.

36:14.111 --> 36:15.020
You have to trust me.

36:15.460 --> 36:17.140
I might not be as gifted as he is,

36:17.820 --> 36:19.740
but I'm more hardworking

36:20.180 --> 36:21.020
and younger.

36:21.700 --> 36:22.660
Most importantly,

36:22.740 --> 36:24.422
I'll be a better partner than he was.

36:25.340 --> 36:25.740
Of course.

36:26.500 --> 36:28.500
I might not surpass the Phantom Knight,

36:28.780 --> 36:30.060
but I'll surpass He Han.

36:30.660 --> 36:31.460
Once I do,

36:31.700 --> 36:32.700
you'll have done it too.

36:33.620 --> 36:35.300
I don't want to hear anyone saying

36:35.820 --> 36:37.333
you're just riding He Han's coattails

36:37.420 --> 36:38.466
or living in his shadow.

36:39.940 --> 36:40.500
Thank you.

36:41.340 --> 36:42.260
But it all starts

36:42.860 --> 36:44.780
with writing those pages every day.

36:50.580 --> 36:54.580
(On Love: Thirty Thousand Chapters,
By the Phantom Knight)

36:56.900 --> 36:57.380
Ms. Lin.

36:59.500 --> 37:00.620
Don't hand me off to anyone.

37:01.940 --> 37:02.940
Zhangzhu is my assistant.

37:03.155 --> 37:05.044
She only handles
the administrative stuff.

37:05.340 --> 37:06.420
I only want to deal with you.

37:07.340 --> 37:07.860
I understand.

37:08.540 --> 37:08.940
Okay.

37:15.860 --> 37:17.220
I'll walk you to your car.

37:17.380 --> 37:18.377
It's fine. Go back inside.

37:18.420 --> 37:19.100
I can manage.

37:19.220 --> 37:19.822
Are you sure?

37:19.940 --> 37:20.380
Yeah.

37:20.740 --> 37:21.020
Bye.

37:21.420 --> 37:21.740
Bye.

37:21.940 --> 37:22.260
Alright.

37:22.460 --> 37:23.133
Get home safe.

37:23.300 --> 37:23.580
Okay.

37:27.580 --> 37:28.822
We've been waiting. Come on.

37:29.460 --> 37:30.380
I'm here, my lady.

37:39.822 --> 37:41.460
So you invited someone over for drinks

37:41.860 --> 37:43.580
and let them snap photos
of the lore book?

37:44.620 --> 37:45.940
No way.

37:46.500 --> 37:46.940
Really?

37:48.180 --> 37:49.420
I don't remember. I'm not sure.

37:49.420 --> 37:50.420
What do you mean?

37:50.420 --> 37:52.300
That editor was a pretty girl,

37:52.900 --> 37:54.660
and she came here,
and you two had a drink.

37:54.660 --> 37:55.540
That's a fact, right?

37:55.740 --> 37:57.100
Yes, she was here.

37:57.340 --> 37:59.060
But only she drank.
I didn't touch a drop.

37:59.180 --> 38:00.860
Besides, you said you were done with me

38:00.860 --> 38:02.380
and told me to find a better editor.

38:02.540 --> 38:04.180
I told you to find an editor,

38:04.180 --> 38:05.580
not a girl.

38:05.700 --> 38:06.940
I wasn't looking for a girl.

38:06.940 --> 38:08.540
The editor just happened to be female.

38:08.688 --> 38:09.540
Aren't you one, too?

38:09.540 --> 38:10.260
So what?

38:10.580 --> 38:12.060
Fine. It's your choice to indulge

38:12.060 --> 38:12.820
in pleasure.

38:12.820 --> 38:13.340
But you can't

38:13.340 --> 38:15.010
let it cause a major mistake at work!

38:15.010 --> 38:16.940
I already told you, I wasn't drinking.

38:16.940 --> 38:17.540
And I wasn't

38:17.540 --> 38:19.180
doing any bad stuff you're imagining.

38:19.300 --> 38:20.780
Of course you wouldn't admit it.

38:20.780 --> 38:22.180
Because I didn't do it!

38:22.180 --> 38:23.100
How did they

38:23.100 --> 38:23.900
snap those photos?

38:24.140 --> 38:25.660
I don't remember, okay? I don't know.

38:25.660 --> 38:26.460
"I don't remember anything."

38:26.460 --> 38:27.911
Is that the best excuse you've got?

38:28.100 --> 38:29.060
Look, maybe she took them

38:29.060 --> 38:30.420
while I was in the bathroom.

38:30.660 --> 38:31.540
Right? I don't know.

38:32.380 --> 38:33.500
Can you stop being angry?

38:33.580 --> 38:34.400
Fine, I admit it.

38:34.500 --> 38:35.420
It's on me.

38:35.420 --> 38:36.860
It's my fault. I'll fix it.

38:37.420 --> 38:38.820
But don't just label me as some guy

38:38.820 --> 38:39.700
who ruins everything

38:39.700 --> 38:40.930
over booze and women.

38:40.930 --> 38:42.177
Is that who you think I am?

38:48.220 --> 38:48.500
Me...

38:49.300 --> 38:50.866
Haven't you messed up enough already?

39:45.580 --> 39:46.340
Have some water.

39:49.380 --> 39:50.311
You're still here?

39:52.820 --> 39:54.180
Stay and talk to me for a bit.

39:55.740 --> 39:56.020
Okay.

39:57.820 --> 39:59.100
Forget the water.

39:59.100 --> 39:59.820
Try this instead.

40:10.940 --> 40:11.620
Mr. He Han...

40:12.260 --> 40:13.660
I've really wanted to write, too.

40:14.380 --> 40:15.460
Do I have what it takes?

40:15.700 --> 40:16.820
Sure. Why not?

40:16.900 --> 40:18.020
Writing is simple.

40:18.780 --> 40:21.260
Did Ms. Lin ever write?

40:21.700 --> 40:22.300
She did,

40:22.820 --> 40:23.820
just not as good as I am.

40:24.140 --> 40:24.980
So, she quit.

40:25.355 --> 40:26.340
If you put it that way,

40:26.340 --> 40:27.980
no one's better than you.

40:27.980 --> 40:28.940
Everyone should give up.

40:29.380 --> 40:30.980
Others don't care, but she does.

40:31.180 --> 40:32.420
Hence, she can't write.

40:34.740 --> 40:35.900
What genre are you into?

40:38.060 --> 40:39.620
I want to write something

40:39.620 --> 40:40.820
that you can't.

40:41.700 --> 40:42.740
Something I can't?

40:43.020 --> 40:44.460
I'm all ears.

40:45.460 --> 40:46.300
Stuff like Mimi's.

40:47.700 --> 40:49.100
Yeah, I can't write that.

40:55.044 --> 40:55.620
Heading out?

40:56.140 --> 40:56.460
Morning.

41:33.220 --> 41:34.260
I'm going to bed.

41:39.620 --> 41:40.420
Morning, Zhao.

41:40.500 --> 41:40.860
Morning.

41:42.980 --> 41:43.660
Where's Wang Hai?

41:44.780 --> 41:45.500
He went to sleep.

41:45.860 --> 41:46.260
Breakfast.

42:25.940 --> 42:26.860
I bought you breakfast.

42:26.860 --> 42:27.780
Get up and eat.

42:28.500 --> 42:29.860
You didn't eat all night.

43:04.977 --> 43:05.777
How old are you?

43:05.955 --> 43:07.380
You don't seem that young anymore.

43:07.540 --> 43:09.466
You need to apologize
for the toxic ideas

43:09.511 --> 43:11.100
you've been feeding my daughter.

43:11.911 --> 43:13.060
What did you say to Zhangzhu?

43:13.177 --> 43:14.422
Her father just came to the office

43:14.444 --> 43:16.266
specifically to give me
a piece of his mind.

43:18.140 --> 43:19.180
It's expensive.

43:20.000 --> 43:20.940
Don't be fooled by how

43:20.940 --> 43:22.540
I like chatting with those young girls.

43:22.820 --> 43:23.580
It's meaningless.

43:25.688 --> 43:27.380
It's one thing for you
to take advantage of me,

43:27.380 --> 43:28.820
but why should I let

43:29.060 --> 43:29.940
other men do it?

43:30.580 --> 43:32.500
Does Lawyer Bei
know what you're really like

43:32.500 --> 43:33.500
in front of your mother?

43:33.780 --> 43:34.260
He doesn't.

43:35.361 --> 43:36.481
(I've been thinking.)

43:37.761 --> 43:41.041
(Everyone's most comfortable level of intimacy)

43:41.801 --> 43:49.131
(is probably different.)

43:50.131 --> 43:51.881
♪If the sky♪

43:52.391 --> 43:53.791
♪And the sea♪

43:54.331 --> 43:56.041
♪Turned upside down♪

43:57.601 --> 43:59.531
♪If a swimming fish♪

43:59.931 --> 44:03.321
♪Fell in love with a flying bird♪

44:05.091 --> 44:07.061
♪If back then♪

44:07.421 --> 44:11.831
♪We had never let go♪

44:12.431 --> 44:18.711
♪We wouldn't be lost in the crowd♪

44:19.831 --> 44:21.981
♪We met in a thirteenth month♪

44:21.981 --> 44:23.851
♪Held each other in a fifth season♪

44:24.031 --> 44:26.471
♪And found our way back whole♪

44:27.311 --> 44:29.481
♪So let this surging love♪

44:29.481 --> 44:33.911
♪Rise like tides that never fall♪

44:34.811 --> 44:36.991
♪If we're caught in a pouring rain♪

44:36.991 --> 44:38.081
♪That's alright♪

44:38.621 --> 44:39.371
♪If we're buried♪

44:39.371 --> 44:42.071
♪By passing years all the better♪

44:42.331 --> 44:44.511
♪At least we still can keep♪

44:44.691 --> 44:49.111
♪This one eternal photograph♪

45:04.871 --> 45:07.161
♪We're on misaligned tracks♪

45:07.161 --> 45:08.921
♪Running in opposite ways♪

45:09.041 --> 45:11.511
♪Searching all along the way♪

45:12.311 --> 45:14.471
♪For the fire of our younger hearts♪

45:14.661 --> 45:19.571
♪And the beauty lost in time♪

45:19.571 --> 45:23.091
♪This time don't lose each other again♪

45:23.331 --> 45:24.301
♪Only after loss♪

45:24.301 --> 45:26.931
♪Do we learn what truly matters most♪

45:27.341 --> 45:29.701
♪In another time and space♪

45:29.701 --> 45:31.261
♪We'll stay and walk together♪

45:31.261 --> 45:34.091
♪Till we grow old♪

45:35.051 --> 45:37.341
♪But still the sky will never♪

45:37.341 --> 45:40.011
♪Turn with the sea♪

45:42.531 --> 45:44.941
♪But still a swimming fish won't♪

45:44.941 --> 45:50.151
♪Fall in love with a flying bird♪
